            <ArticleTitle>Thrombosis of the left coronary artery in a newborn infant.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>957-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A unique occurrence of antenatal thrombosis of the left main coronary artery in a term infant is presented. The clinical features are indistinguishable from those of several other forms of congenital heart disease. The etiology of the thrombosis is unknown.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
